path: /contact
title: Contact The School Manager: talk to a person in Pakistan
description: A small team in Pakistan. Ring, message the WhatsApp number or email, and somebody who knows the software answers rather than a sales script.
nav_order: 20
breadcrumb: Contact
schema: org
priority: 0.7
---

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
    <h1>Who you are calling</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width:64ch">
      A small team in Pakistan. Ring the number and a person who knows the software answers. If you would rather see it than read about it, we will walk one class through with you on a call.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tint" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <div class="card" style="text-align: center; padding: 40px 24px;">
        <div class="card__icon" style="margin: 0 auto 16px;">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Phone</h3>
        <p><a class="clink" id="contact-phone" hidden href="#"></a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="text-align: center; padding: 40px 24px;">
        <div class="card__icon card__icon--accent" style="margin: 0 auto 16px;">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 12h.01M12 12h.01M16 12h.01M21 12c0 4.418-4.03 8-9 8a9.863 9.863 0 01-4.255-.949L3 20l1.395-3.72C3.512 15.042 3 13.574 3 12c0-4.418 4.03-8 9-8s9 3.582 9 8z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>WhatsApp</h3>
        <p><a class="clink" id="contact-whatsapp" hidden href="#" rel="noopener"></a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="text-align: center; padding: 40px 24px;">
        <div class="card__icon" style="background: var(--due-50); color: var(--due-800); margin: 0 auto 16px;">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Email</h3>
        <p><a class="clink" id="contact-email" hidden href="#"></a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p id="contact-todo" hidden class="small" style="margin-top:16px;color:var(--due-800); text-align: center;">
      Set CONTACT_PHONE, CONTACT_WHATSAPP and CONTACT_EMAIL in config.js on the deployment. A page this careful with an unset phone number is worse than a plain page with a real one.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What a first call covers</h2>
    <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:22px">
      <li>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>Your own fee structure, in your own words, against what the software can hold. If it cannot hold something, you find out on the call.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>Moving the records you already have. Bring a sample of your spreadsheet and we will tell you honestly how much of it imports cleanly.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span>One month of challans for one class, run beside your existing register, so the decision is made on your numbers rather than on a demonstration.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
